1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,753
SiteWitness brings site context, photographs, human
observations and AI suggestions into one inspection.

2
00:00:07,753 --> 00:00:13,142
This public Preview opens without a judge account,
invitation or access code.

3
00:00:13,142 --> 00:00:19,715
For this recording, we reuse a clearly labeled, previously
captured Muse Spark result.

4
00:00:19,715 --> 00:00:25,814
That genuine response came from this construction
photograph; no new model call is made.

5
00:00:25,814 --> 00:00:33,232
The provenance panel records Muse Spark 1.3, response
checks, image hash and capture details.

6
00:00:33,232 --> 00:00:38,265
We edit the earlier AI wording and record a human decision
with a follow-up note.

7
00:00:38,265 --> 00:00:44,139
Saving this example to the browser lets the unified
workspace import its genuine result.

8
00:00:44,139 --> 00:00:49,857
The unified workspace keeps that captured report and
photograph in one inspection record.

9
00:00:49,857 --> 00:00:54,780
We add site context and a human summary before making a
review decision.

10
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:59,424
This is the exact photograph used for the saved Muse Spark
response.

11
00:00:59,424 --> 00:01:04,392
We add a human observation about visible bracing without
claiming stability.

12
00:01:04,392 --> 00:01:09,801
Human observations and AI suggestions have separate labels
in the findings list.

13
00:01:09,801 --> 00:01:14,919
Now we compare the AI suggestion with the photograph and its
stated limitation.

14
00:01:14,919 --> 00:01:20,523
The human observation keeps its supporting evidence and
limits beside AI suggestions.

15
00:01:20,523 --> 00:01:24,831
Labels keep human review distinct from the model's original
output.

16
00:01:24,831 --> 00:01:29,995
The inspection saves to this browser profile with its photo
and AI provenance.

17
00:01:29,995 --> 00:01:35,273
After reopening, the edited description and review decision
are still present.

18
00:01:35,273 --> 00:01:41,287
The printable report brings site details, human notes, the
photo and findings together.

19
00:01:41,287 --> 00:01:46,875
Its AI source, review status and limitations remain readable
in the PDF.

20
00:01:46,875 --> 00:01:53,234
This is a previously captured result; new photographs need a
new user-initiated analysis.

21
00:01:53,234 --> 00:01:58,727
No segmentation masks or pixel-level localization are
claimed in this workflow.

22
00:01:58,727 --> 00:02:05,701
The report is preliminary visual documentation, not
engineering certification or a safety verdict.

23
00:02:05,701 --> 00:02:12,519
Browser-local records do not sync across devices; export a
backup before clearing browser data.

24
00:02:12,519 --> 00:02:19,237
SiteWitness preserves evidence for review, while qualified
people remain responsible for decisions.
